---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_URL } from "../data/site";

const CONTACT_PHONE_DISPLAY = "0475 624 247";
const CONTACT_PHONE_TEL = "+61475624247";
const LAST_UPDATED = "8 October 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Screwdriver Marketing"
  description="How Screwdriver Marketing collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal information when you use our website, forms, quizzes, or contact us."
>
  <div class="relative min-h-screen overflow-x-hidden">
    <header class="relative z-10 border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-bg-deep">
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
        <a href="/" class="font-display text-lg font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-xl">
          Screwdriver <span class="text-accent">Marketing</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/" class="text-sm font-medium text-muted transition hover:text-cream">← Back to home</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="relative z-10 px-5 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
      <article class="legal-prose mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="font-display mt-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

        <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed">
          Screwdriver Marketing (ABN 47 337 145 828), based in Adelaide, South Australia, respects your privacy and is committed to handling personal information responsibly.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose and protect personal information through our website, advertising campaigns, enquiries and marketing services, including information processed on behalf of our business clients.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We may collect the following personal and business information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Name and business name</li>
          <li>Email address and phone number</li>
          <li>Website or Google Business Profile details</li>
          <li>Business location, services and marketing requirements</li>
          <li>Information submitted through forms, quizzes, audits, enquiries or bookings</li>
          <li>Billing, transaction and service-related information</li>
          <li>Communications and interactions with our business</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may also collect website usage information through cookies, analytics tools and advertising technologies, including device information, approximate location, pages visited and advertising interactions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information may be collected directly through our website, Facebook and Instagram lead forms, referrals, publicly available business listings, third-party integrations and other lawful sources.
        </p>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We may use personal information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to enquiries and provide requested information, quotes or audits</li>
          <li>Contact prospective customers about our services</li>
          <li>Deliver website, marketing, reputation management and automation services</li>
          <li>Manage appointments, client accounts, payments and communications</li>
          <li>Send relevant marketing communications where permitted by law</li>
          <li>Improve our website, services and advertising campaigns</li>
          <li>Maintain business records and meet legal obligations</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may contact you through phone, SMS or email, subject to applicable consent and marketing requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Marketing Communications</h2>
        <p>
          If you enquire about our services, submit a form or otherwise provide your contact information, we may contact you regarding your enquiry and relevant services.
        </p>
        <p>
          Marketing communications are sent in accordance with applicable Australian laws, including the Spam Act 2003.
        </p>
        <p>You can opt out of marketing communications at any time by:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Replying STOP to marketing SMS messages</li>
          <li>Using the unsubscribe link in marketing emails</li>
          <li>Contacting us directly</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We will respect valid unsubscribe requests and applicable consent requirements.</p>

        <h2>4. Client Customer Information</h2>
        <p>
          As part of our marketing and reputation management services, Screwdriver Marketing may process personal information on behalf of business clients.
        </p>
        <p>This information may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Customer names and contact details</li>
          <li>Service and transaction information</li>
          <li>Appointment or purchase history</li>
          <li>Customer feedback and review activity</li>
          <li>Information transferred through CRM, accounting, booking or other integrated systems</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We use this information to provide services requested by our clients, including customer review requests, follow-ups, reputation management and agreed marketing automations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Business clients are responsible for ensuring they have appropriate authority to provide customer information and instruct us to process it, including obtaining any consent required by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Screwdriver Marketing is independently responsible for meeting its own applicable privacy, security and marketing obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell client customer information or use it for unrelated marketing purposes without appropriate authorisation.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies, Analytics and Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Our website may use cookies, tracking pixels and analytics technologies to understand visitor activity, improve website performance, measure advertising effectiveness and support marketing campaigns.
        </p>
        <p>These technologies may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Analytics</li>
          <li>Google Tag Manager</li>
          <li>Meta Pixel</li>
          <li>Website analytics and hosting tools</li>
          <li>CRM and marketing automation technologies</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Third-party providers may process information in accordance with their own privacy policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings, although this may affect certain website features.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
        <p>
          We may share personal information with trusted third-party providers where reasonably necessary to operate our business and deliver services.
        </p>
        <p>These may include providers of:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>CRM and marketing automation software, including GoHighLevel</li>
          <li>Email and SMS communications</li>
          <li>Website hosting and analytics</li>
          <li>Advertising and social media platforms</li>
          <li>Payment processing, including Stripe</li>
          <li>Accounting, booking and business administration tools</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information to third parties.</p>
        <p>
          Information may also be disclosed where required or authorised by law, or where reasonably necessary to investigate fraud, security incidents or unlawful activity.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Overseas Data Processing</h2>
        <p>
          Some third-party service providers may store or process personal information outside Australia, including in the United States.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where applicable, we take reasonable steps to protect personal information handled by overseas service providers and meet our obligations under Australian privacy law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Overseas providers may be subject to different privacy and data protection laws.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Information Security</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect personal information against misuse, interference, loss, unauthorised access, modification and disclosure.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use third-party platforms and systems to store and process information as part of our operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          While we seek to protect the information we handle, no electronic system or transmission method can be guaranteed completely secure.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide services, manage business relationships, fulfil the purposes described in this policy and meet legal obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          When information is no longer required, we take reasonable steps to delete or de-identify it, subject to applicable recordkeeping requirements and technical limitations, including backup systems.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Access, Correction and Deletion</h2>
        <p>You may contact us to request:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access to personal information we hold about you</li>
          <li>Correction of inaccurate or outdated information</li>
          <li>Deletion of personal information where appropriate</li>
          <li>Withdrawal of marketing consent</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We will consider and respond to requests in accordance with applicable law.</p>
        <p>
          Where information is processed on behalf of another business, we may need to refer your request to that business.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Data Breaches</h2>
        <p>
          If we become aware of a suspected data breach involving personal information, we will take appropriate steps to investigate, assess and contain the incident.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where required by applicable law, we will notify affected individuals and relevant authorities, including the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).
        </p>

        <h2>12. Privacy Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you have concerns about how your personal information has been handled, please contact us using the details below.
        </p>
        <p>We will review your complaint and respond within a reasonable timeframe.</p>
        <p>
          If you are dissatisfied with our response, you may be able to lodge a complaint with the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.oaic.gov.au</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our services, business practices or legal obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          The latest version will be published on our website with an updated revision date.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>For privacy enquiries, requests, complaints or marketing opt-outs, please contact:</p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-cream">Screwdriver Marketing</strong><br />
          ABN: 47 337 145 828<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a><br />
          Phone: <a href={CONTACT_PHONE_TEL}>{CONTACT_PHONE_DISPLAY}</a><br />
          Location: Adelaide, South Australia<br />
          Website: <a href={SITE_URL}>{SITE_URL}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-syne);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal-prose ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal-prose li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-prose a {
    color: var(--signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal-prose a:hover {
    color: var(--cream);
  }
</style>
